definitions.documentation:
Xero Response Metadata is a versioned Xero data block. Core fields are typed and provider-owned additional fields are preserved. Example: 

```json
{
  "status": 200,
  "minuteRemaining": "59",
  "dayRemaining": "999"
}
```

JSON Schema is enforced at sockets. Optional fields stay absent; they are not filled from schema defaults. [Xero accounting requests](https://developer.xero.com/documentation/api/accounting/requests-and-responses/), [OAuth tokens](https://developer.xero.com/documentation/guides/oauth2/token-types/), [tenant connections](https://developer.xero.com/documentation/guides/oauth2/tenants/), [idempotency](https://developer.xero.com/documentation/guides/idempotent-requests/idempotency/), [rate limits](https://developer.xero.com/documentation/best-practices/api-call-efficiencies/rate-limits/).

## Audited socket contract (21 October 2026)

Inputs:
No data sockets.

Outputs:
No data sockets.

Configuration:
No asset-specific configuration.

Known provider records and list elements have structural schemas. Explicit dynamic payloads, selected query results and provider extensions retain the recursive JSON Value vocabulary; they do not imply a known provider entity. Null is distinct from omission. Runtime validates the exact selected immutable type version; reading newer documentation never repins existing graphs. This audit used synthetic fixtures/local mocks and does not establish live provider authorization or delivery.

Authoritative JSON Schema:

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "status": {
      "type": "number"
    },
    "correlationId": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "minuteRemaining": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "dayRemaining": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "appMinuteRemaining": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "retryAfterSeconds": {
      "type": "number"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "status"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

Library registry key: `xero.metadata`.
